{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned","id":969937,"title":"The Technocracy and Indoctrination of the none-Awakned","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-15T08:33:57-07:00","id":969937,"title":"The Technocracy and Indoctrination of the none-Awakned","content":"Does the Technocracy brainwash and utilize other captured supernaturals beside the Mages? It should be very easy and handy, when compared, so to speak, brainwash Hermetic, Chorus or Akashayana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 09-15-2016, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:54:47-07:00","id":969954,"title":"","content":"I've never seen it mentioned. What kind of creatures did you have in mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:21:19-07:00","id":969977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=969954#post969954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never seen it mentioned. What kind of creatures did you have in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every other supernatural creature except the Mage, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T10:48:20-07:00","id":970030,"title":"","content":"While it'd be an interesting flourish for a given story, on the whole I'd imagine they're just too volatile to be worth the effort.<br /> <br /> Mages are stubborn but they're not <i>supernaturally furious </i>like a vampire or werewolf, nor do they have an evil psychic twin like a wraith or KJ, and indoctrination is probably just fatally banal to a changeling. Plus if you start snatching vampires off the street they're liable to return the favor, and the garou are going to mount a rescue operation with their furry SEAL operatives (but not their seal operatives, which were wiped out in the War of Rage.) Both of these are Bad For Business in ways that turning the competition really isn't.<br /> <br /> And, due to my incredible prescience, I will note that &quot;well obviously to neuter the Beast/Rage you just need to roll even more successes&quot; is going to get ignored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T10:53:54-07:00","id":970041,"title":"","content":"Changelings would be difficult, as even being around Technocrats is physically deleterious because of their incredible ambient Banality, and the necessary levels of Conditioning would almost certainly destroy their Fae mein. Conversely though it might be possible (and horrifying) for the Technocracy to do such a thing deliberately with the intent of creating special Dauntain shock troops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T11:10:11-07:00","id":970050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=970030#post970030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it'd be an interesting flourish for a given story, on the whole I'd imagine they're just too volatile to be worth the effort.<br /> <br /> Mages are stubborn but they're not <i>supernaturally furious </i>like a vampire or werewolf, nor do they have an evil psychic twin like a wraith or KJ, and indoctrination is probably just fatally banal to a changeling. Plus if you start snatching vampires off the street they're liable to return the favor, and the garou are going to mount a rescue operation with their furry SEAL operatives (but not their seal operatives, which were wiped out in the War of Rage.) Both of these are Bad For Business in ways that turning the competition really isn't.<br /> <br /> And, due to my incredible prescience, I will note that &quot;well obviously to neuter the Beast/Rage you just need to roll even more successes&quot; is going to get ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if vampires or werewolves desire to get revenge of their friends, how they can hope to track and uncover indoctrination facilities? Especially if the said facilities are established in the Horizon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T11:10:38-07:00","id":970052,"title":"","content":"It might be possible for werewolves, since they're just as susceptible to mental illness and probably eve conditioning. Hell, they have a while facility dedicated to werewolves who can't quite handle the reality of their existence as shapeshifters, with the purpose of rehabilitating them. I'd say that it's possible to go the other way with it, capture, condition, and utilize as shock troops. They are not going to be terribly useful otherwise though. Even reconditioned Tradition mages maintain a tenuous connection to said conditioning and are under constant supervision. Hell, they're even more likely to act in suicidal manners when on missions, subconsciously aware that something is wrong and maybe death is a release. To do something similar to a religious zealot like a werewolf, particularly one that has witnessed proof of their belief, it might be even worse. Think caged animals dropped into a battlefield to be released to do the most amount of indiscriminate damage.<br /> <br /> Vampires... maybe. They're susceptible to other forms of mystical brainwashing, ie Dominate and the blood bond, so it's not inconceivable that some high level Mind Procedures could do the same. You're still going to have to take care of the feeding of the thing though, and if any local Kindred court catches wind of your pet leech, there's going to be questions, at the very least.<br /> <br /> I can't speak much to the others, but in any case, the Technocracy would have to be in some pretty dire straits to use such dangerous Reality Deviants and not simply dispose of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T11:38:30-07:00","id":970070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=970050#post970050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if vampires or werewolves desire to get revenge of their friends, how they can hope to track and uncover indoctrination facilities? Especially if the said facilities are established in the Horizon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best part about taking retribution on an organization is that you're not obligated to take revenge on the specific people responsible for vexing you. The Union has vast immobile Earthside assets and operatives who cannot be withdrawn to the safety of secure facilities without ceding the Front Lines - which, as their name suggests, are seen as vital to the Union's efforts. How many Syndicate businesses and Progenitor research labs is a Kindred operative worth? How many non-Enlightened personnel? Do we move everyone's families Horizon-side too? The kindred court's not going to want their guy back<i>, they hate that guy, </i>but they have a political obligation to extract a blood-price for stepping on their toes, and vampires are experts at vendettas.<br /> <br /> Werewolves just Pulse of the Prey and hunt <i>anyone</i> <i>anywhere</i>, because it is dumb to pick a fight with werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:07:30-07:00","id":970089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=970050#post970050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if vampires or werewolves desire to get revenge of their friends, how they can hope to track and uncover indoctrination facilities? Especially if the said facilities are established in the Horizon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about werewolves, but vampires don't want to get revenge for their friends (except when blood-ties are involved). They just hate it when vampires serve other entities, because it somehow hurts their ego...They hunt down infernalists, not the demons. They will hunt the brainwashed vampire, not the technos (though they won't spit on the opportunity of wrecking havoc on them).<br /> <br /> As for indoctrination, I don't know how it would be possible with werewolves. But for vampires, you can indoctrinate them (just like they get indoctrinated by other vampires).<br /> The problem is that their mind is separate from their blood. You can rape their minds, but the blood of Caine remains its own.<br /> <br /> That means that no matter how successful your indoctrination is, even if the vampire is 100% head over heels for the Technos, there will be a time when he'll betray them. Not because the indoctrination failed, but because it's in their nature. It's never explained why, it just seems to come from their curse.<br /> <br /> Even when they are blood-bond to a vampire, vinculumed to a pack, tied to a kuei-Jin or chained to a Decani, even if some knight gave his word of oath. They can't help but entertain ideas of betrayal. The only way they can avoid betrayal is through suicide.<br /> <br /> So, the only way to keep them loyal is through fear. Like the Sabbat does, they make sure anyone who fails the sect (one way or the other) doesn't get killed, instead they give them the worst treatment imaginable.<br /> <br /> The remaining problem is that it goes both ways. Both Sabbat and Camarilla torture their traitors but they also reserve the same treatment to aberrations who serve demons or other entities (like the technos). That means by threatening the vampire to serve you, you trap him between his fear of the technos and his fear of other vampires. So, even then, you're not 100% sure he'll chose you over the other (if, he hasn't committed suicide already...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:47:37-07:00","id":970245,"title":"","content":"It's much more convenient to take the supernaturals apart, use their organs as xenografts, and create custom-engineered lifeforms as shock troops than to deal with the baggage of a nerve-stapled freeborn Deviant. They're significantly less pliable than humans, for all the mentioned reasons.<br /> <br /> If you really want highly expendable paranormal shock troops, there's also the option to just make a couple baseline clones and use V-blood to transform them into proper hemophages.<br /> <br /> Of course, if the Glass Walkers, Bone Gnawers, or possibly some hemophages decided to join of their own free choice as full members and be subject to standard re-education policies, well, that's a different story there, now isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:02:17-07:00","id":970255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=970052#post970052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be possible for werewolves, since they're just as susceptible to mental illness and probably eve conditioning. Hell, they have a while facility dedicated to werewolves who can't quite handle the reality of their existence as shapeshifters, with the purpose of rehabilitating them. I'd say that it's possible to go the other way with it, capture, condition, and utilize as shock troops. They are not going to be terribly useful otherwise though. Even reconditioned Tradition mages maintain a tenuous connection to said conditioning and are under constant supervision. Hell, they're even more likely to act in suicidal manners when on missions, subconsciously aware that something is wrong and maybe death is a release. To do something similar to a religious zealot like a werewolf</div> </div> </div> </div>They probably don't seem anywhere nearly like that to people who can also see spirits and know what spirits are like, in the context of &quot;they are close to these beings&quot;. Then they just become frighteningly intense people who are in an awful lot of beneficial relationships with otherworldly entities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> , particularly one that has witnessed proof of their belief, it might be even worse. Think caged animals dropped into a battlefield to be released to do the most amount of indiscriminate damage.<br /> <br /> Vampires... maybe. They're susceptible to other forms of mystical brainwashing, ie Dominate and the blood bond, so it's not inconceivable that some high level Mind Procedures could do the same. You're still going to have to take care of the feeding of the thing though, and if any local Kindred court catches wind of your pet leech, there's going to be questions, at the very least.<br /> <br /> I can't speak much to the others, but in any case, the Technocracy would have to be in some pretty dire straits to use such dangerous Reality Deviants and not simply dispose of them. </div> </div> </div>You wouldn't want to try with werewolves, for a reason very similar to why vampires probably wouldn't want to try blood bonding them if they knew what they were like - Garou and Fera, with two exceptions, tend to have emotions that are frighteningly intense as part and parcel of the Rage that makes them so good at killing shit in a fight. The end product would be so yandere for the mission statement that you'd probably end up begging for un-adjusted werebeasts again... while on the run, trying to avoid a shapeshifting Yuno Gasai who can track you by your heartbeat no matter where you happen to be, among other frightening capabilities like being able to duplicate anyone's appearance or making anything technological stop working.<br /> <br /> As for the ones that don't have Rage... the Ananasi would probably just turn into spiders and scuttle off to eat your family, while Nuwisha would probably have you at your wits' end with their &quot;teaching&quot; methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:52:51-07:00","id":970425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=970070#post970070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The best part about taking retribution on an organization is that you're not obligated to take revenge on the specific people responsible for vexing you. The Union has vast immobile Earthside assets and operatives who cannot be withdrawn to the safety of secure facilities without ceding the Front Lines - which, as their name suggests, are seen as vital to the Union's efforts. How many Syndicate businesses and Progenitor research labs is a Kindred operative worth? How many non-Enlightened personnel? Do we move everyone's families Horizon-side too? The kindred court's not going to want their guy back<i>, they hate that guy, </i>but they have a political obligation to extract a blood-price for stepping on their toes, and vampires are experts at vendettas.<br /> <br /> Werewolves just Pulse of the Prey and hunt <i>anyone</i> <i>anywhere</i>, because it is dumb to pick a fight with werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how could the Vampire possibly find and track down the Syndicate businesses, Progenitor research labs and families of agents? And how they could get through guards and security systems undetected and unobstructed and proceed to massacre un-Enlightened personnel, especially if they are well-armed and well-protected?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T20:01:56-07:00","id":970433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=970425#post970425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how could the Vampire possibly find and track down the Syndicate businesses, Progenitor research labs and families of agents? And how they could get through guards and security systems undetected and unobstructed and proceed to massacre un-Enlightened personnel, especially if they are well-armed and well-protected?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This could lead us down the road that the Technocracy vs. Vampries thread has gone. I think it might be wise to leave that discussion over there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T22:27:23-07:00","id":970499,"title":"","content":"Active and continuous Mind Control is a horrible inefficient way to direct volatile assets. Much safer to have a handler and a few key words as back up. and leverage. Lots of leverage. Basically play the vampire game against the asset. You will do this because 1) I have your dirty secretes in my hand 2) my words have reality defining power and 3) You're getting paid for it<br /> <br /> Always fund your asset, especially if you value it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T01:48:20-07:00","id":970574,"title":"","content":"If you aren't in a state where you need to fully usurp control of the asset's will, Conditioning is the go-to &quot;mind control&quot; power, and is well-supported by Union infrastructure to the point it's not a substantive cost. Coupled with, yes, the usual soft power for non-expendable assets.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, no amount of leverage or other soft power will help you, because <i>they are in Frenzy</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T03:37:57-07:00","id":970609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=970425#post970425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how could the Vampire possibly find and track down the Syndicate businesses, Progenitor research labs and families of agents?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a question, what are you planning to do with the captives after brainwashing them?<br /> <br /> I previously talked with the assumption that you were planning to use them as something more than just test subjects or lab decorations.<br /> <br /> But, the way you're saying it, I get the feeling you want to lock them up in the facilities or labs...which is fine. But then what's the point of brainwashing them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-16-2016, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T05:30:44-07:00","id":970638,"title":"","content":"Intelligence against related targets? Beyond that, I do not see why they would want one. It is much easier to transform a mortal into a Drone, which can manifest any supernatural power their Creator wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T11:05:41-07:00","id":970788,"title":"","content":"Is it just me or is anyone else kind of getting annoyed by the idea that powers will solve all the problems? Like to the point where mundane solutions are looked down on? It's kind of feeling like people just want to play with their new toys. When really the marrying of mundane practices and secrete powers is still very powerful. A little bit of leg work really does enhance the effectiveness of your powers.<br /> <br /> I mean just look at the mechainics, You can get bonuses for tools and incorporating methods into your magic. Both the magic and the mundane can compliment each other. Not to mention its less of an exp sink. so lowbie mages can still rock out against masters. It's all about prep work and espionage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:47:44-07:00","id":970894,"title":"","content":"Of course. I also think that people forget how effective exceptional mortals are against the supernatural. I would not bet against a SF A-team, even if they were facing a group of Mages. Since there are 7,000 SF personnel in the USA, that makes them over twice as common as Mages in the USA","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:10:43-07:00","id":971374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=970609#post970609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just a question, what are you planning to do with the captives after brainwashing them?<br /> <br /> I previously talked with the assumption that you were planning to use them as something more than just test subjects or lab decorations.<br /> <br /> But, the way you're saying it, I get the feeling you want to lock them up in the facilities or labs...which is fine. But then what's the point of brainwashing them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course I am proposing to use them as brainwashed agents. Why on earth do you think I want to lock them up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:15:26-07:00","id":971379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=970894#post970894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course. I also think that people forget how effective exceptional mortals are against the supernatural. I would not bet against a SF A-team, even if they were facing a group of Mages. Since there are 7,000 SF personnel in the USA, that makes them over twice as common as Mages in the USA</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not catching on what are you trying to say. Since that is exactly my rebuttal against hopeful reverie that &quot;Vampires will rampage through un-Enlightened personnel! Vampires ROCK!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:44:50-07:00","id":971398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=971374#post971374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course I am proposing to use them as brainwashed agents. Why on earth do you think I want to lock them up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you keep asking how others will track them down.<br /> If you plan to use them as agents, they are bound to be exposed at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:19:54-07:00","id":973935,"title":"","content":"You could gather the successes needed in an extended interrogation session. Cainites have easily exploitable weakness of blood carving. Something like a mind control chip or regular mind-control sessions would need to be done, and something to keep frenzy at bay, and something to stop the Cainite from becoming a Wight. What you get in return is Paradox-free enhanced agent.<br /> <br /> Garou would be useful because of Delirium and Umbra capabilities.<br /> <br /> I can see Wraiths and Spectres being controllable through a specialized Postmortem Entities Psychology field. (Possibly backed by Dimensional Science equipment). Identifying the Passions, the nature of the Shadow, acquiring or creating new Fetters, feeding Pathos and managing Angst, helping develop Arcanoi... And the equivalent stuff for Spectres. Might even try to Redeem them.<br /> (The world's most accomplished necromancer is actually not a Giovanni or a Nagaraja, but 300 or so years old Technocrat, currently heading the Watchers.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-21-2016, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T13:51:22-07:00","id":974011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=973935#post973935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(The world's most accomplished necromancer is actually not a Giovanni or a Nagaraja, but 300 or so years old Technocrat, currently heading the Watchers.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Paramaguru Voormas or Japheth might raise some objections about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-21-2016, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T20:40:41-07:00","id":974208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=973935#post973935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could gather the successes needed in an extended interrogation session. Cainites have easily exploitable weakness of blood carving. Something like a mind control chip or regular mind-control sessions would need to be done, and something to keep frenzy at bay, and something to stop the Cainite from becoming a Wight. What you get in return is Paradox-free enhanced agent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, just the 'don't frenzy as much' and 'avoid dealing with Humanity loss' mods would make this an <i>amazing</i> deal for a lot of vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T09:13:47-07:00","id":974455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=974208#post974208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, just the 'don't frenzy as much' and 'avoid dealing with Humanity loss' mods would make this an <i>amazing</i> deal for a lot of vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a question though of how to actually accomplish that. Frenzy and rotschreck are fairly straightforward, as they usually operates off of triggers, the responses to which can be fiddled with using Mind. Inuring them to effects which induce frenzy or rotschreck is more complicated, but making a &quot;basic&quot; frenzy-free vampire wouldn't be too hard. <br /> <br /> &quot;[...]something to stop the Cainite from becoming Wight&quot; is <i>considerably</i> more complicated, as you start dealing more directly with the beast. The beast is nebulous and tends to defy efforts to quantify it, something which is probably going to frustrate Enlightened Science. I'm not saying its impossible, but the magical effect is going to have be much more involved and complex. Then there's how to actually prevent the slide into wassail. Messing with stimuli responses like with frenzy and rotschreck isn't going to work because removing guilt tends to actually accelerate degeneration. What you would need to do is to basically create a new Path of Enlightenment that is taylored to your needs and coerce the vampire into adopting it. The downsides of this are that they will still have a number of behavioral ticks (in the form of Path sins) which may make them unwieldy agents, and in order to do this one would need to do some fairly deep research into Path lore to understand its underlying relationship to the beast and soul. That's pretty much the only way that's happening though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:11:59-07:00","id":974545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=974455#post974455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a question though of how to actually accomplish that. Frenzy and rotschreck are fairly straightforward, as they usually operates off of triggers, the responses to which can be fiddled with using Mind. Inuring them to effects which induce frenzy or rotschreck is more complicated, but making a &quot;basic&quot; frenzy-free vampire wouldn't be too hard.<br /> <br /> &quot;[...]something to stop the Cainite from becoming Wight&quot; is <i>considerably</i> more complicated, as you start dealing more directly with the beast. The beast is nebulous and tends to defy efforts to quantify it, something which is probably going to frustrate Enlightened Science. I'm not saying its impossible, but the magical effect is going to have be much more involved and complex. Then there's how to actually prevent the slide into wassail. Messing with stimuli responses like with frenzy and rotschreck isn't going to work because removing guilt tends to actually accelerate degeneration. What you would need to do is to basically create a new Path of Enlightenment that is taylored to your needs and coerce the vampire into adopting it. The downsides of this are that they will still have a number of behavioral ticks (in the form of Path sins) which may make them unwieldy agents, and in order to do this one would need to do some fairly deep research into Path lore to understand its underlying relationship to the beast and soul. That's pretty much the only way that's happening though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, actually <i>permanently</i> dealing with the Beast would be a hefty order to fill, requiring <i>at least</i> Mind 5 (to essentially restructure the basic nature of the vampiric mind). Restoring Humanity already lost might require similar levels, or perhaps perhaps Mind 4 to restore their conscious mind's memories to a state of innocence (I might rule that removing the karmic guilt/Resonance of the act itself might warrant conjunctional Prime). This might give the dots directly, or just ease purchasing it back up with experience, either reducing the amount a la Life 4 per Verbena Revised, or obviating the 'training time'.<br /> <br /> The easier method would be to use a Dominate-equivalent Mind 4 effect to attempt to control the vampire during a frenzy, or to use a Mind 2 emotional stabilizer to effectively reduce the difficulty of frenzy/rotschreck rolls (-3 diff to Self-Control or Courage rolls would do a heck of a lot there, putting them at similar difficulties to a Ghoul). Something like a Buffy-style morality chip might - <i>if</i> the designer in question understood the vampiric condition enough to understand that justification and repression is the opposite of what's needed - be able to do similar things for conscience rolls, inclining them towards a sense of remorse for inHuman actions.<br /> <br /> As implants, these can essentially be a permanent-effect Device, and as rank-2 effects they'd be reasonably cheap to make for a few exceptionally useful vampiric agents. As far as Devices go, that is.<br /> <br /> Extraordinary Citizens might be able to make similar things, since these are relatively low-end and fairly Coincidental effects.<br /> <br /> ...Yeah I've been thinking about how Revenant Mages might work a lot lately, and that carries over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:22:57-07:00","id":974552,"title":"","content":"The only problem with chips and implants is that vampiric bodies reject any permanent alteration to their physical form that isn't performed with Vicissitude (and even that's sort of nebulous on whether it works with foreign matter or not). Why that specifically works and nothing else is never really explored, but if you wanted to make an implant work you would probably have to hack the underlying principles of Vicissitude first. Or in reverse figure out the deeper reasons why vampiric bodies are so static and figure out a way to magic around it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 09-22-2016, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:37:37-07:00","id":974559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=974552#post974552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only problem with chips and implants is that vampiric bodies reject any permanent alteration to their physical form that isn't performed with Vicissitude (and even that's sort of nebulous on whether it works with foreign matter or not). Why that specifically works and nothing else is never really explored, but if you wanted to make an implant work you would probably have to hack the underlying principles of Vicissitude first. Or in reverse figure out the deeper reasons why vampiric bodies are so static and figure out a way to magic around it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think that making an implant Device - which has its own innate magick maintaining its existence and integration with the body - might get around that. Alternatively, get a Thaumaturge who's familiar with the Brand ritual from Rites of the Blood. It's a Rank One ritual - anyone who has any Thaumaturgy at all can learn it or potentially develop it on their own. It specifically causes body modifications, tattoos, etc. applied within the past hour to be permanently made part of the vampire's 'default' state.<br /> <br /> Hurts like hell, but hey, it works.<br /> <br /> There are other methods, as well; an NWO psychiatrist with Prime 4/Mind 2 and appropriate Tass could enchant the vampire as a Living Talisman. Avoiding affecting the body may well be sufficient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:04:33-07:00","id":974651,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, you could try to avoid Degeneration by implanting deep directives against the worst Sins on the Humanity hierarchy. Given that the bottom two ranks include &quot;Thoughtless Killing and feeding past satiation&quot;, and &quot;Utter Perversion or heinous acts&quot; (V20, p. 312), it's the sort of activity the Technocracy would want to prevent their agent from doing <i>anyway</i>. And if they can't perform those sins, they can't lose those last precious dots of Humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:40:48-07:00","id":974676,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't the innate countermagic of the Kindred cause any magical effects to fail pretty quickly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T15:01:04-07:00","id":974685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=974651#post974651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, you could try to avoid Degeneration by implanting deep directives against the worst Sins on the Humanity hierarchy. Given that the bottom two ranks include &quot;Thoughtless Killing and feeding past satiation&quot;, and &quot;Utter Perversion or heinous acts&quot; (V20, p. 312), it's the sort of activity the Technocracy would want to prevent their agent from doing <i>anyway</i>. And if they can't perform those sins, they can't lose those last precious dots of Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I agree that the Technocracy is against thoughtless killing or heinous act. We 'are' talking about them trying to make a brainwashed vampire agent, which is already pretty deep in the weeds. Moreover, for what other purpose would they even want to have such an agent if not for deniable acts of morally repugnant skulduggery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T16:04:18-07:00","id":974718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=974685#post974685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I agree that the Technocracy is against thoughtless killing or heinous act. We 'are' talking about them trying to make a brainwashed vampire agent, which is already pretty deep in the weeds. Moreover, for what other purpose would they even want to have such an agent if not for deniable acts of morally repugnant skulduggery?</div> </div> </div> </div>Note I said &quot;<i>thoughtless</i> killing&quot;, not &quot;premeditated murder&quot;. The sin to which I refer is killing that is done casually, without consideration for the consequences. While the Technocracy isn't above a tactical assassination or the like, they tend to prefer not to have a psychopath running around who kills for any reason, or even no reason. The Union is about control.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it another way, I'm advocating the Union mind whack their hemophage agent to never kill unless either ordered to by a superior, or as a matter of self defense. Anything else on those levels of Humanity - feeding beyond what the vampire needs to survive, or committing gross acts of vile evil - are neither necessary nor desired by the Technocracy. Despite that the Union is willing to do what's needed, they don't tend to see themselves as monsters. Or, at the very least, abject monstrosity causes more problems than they solve, when you're trying to maintain a Consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:19:24-07:00","id":974768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=974676#post974676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't the innate countermagic of the Kindred cause any magical effects to fail pretty quickly?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... not actually a thing?<br /> <br /> Night-Folk in general as of M20 (specifically M20) can use Occult to perform active countermagic. Thaumaturgy also allows them to countermagic under some rulings. But those are both active countermeasures based on mystical knowledge. It requires recognition that something's going on, that it's magical, and a decision on the vampire's part to oppose it. Furthermore, as a Knowledge, if they don't actually have Occult, they can't do anything.<br /> <br /> If the effect is applied with their permission, or the vampire doesn't have the above means at hand, it's not going to spontaneously stop just because &quot;lol vampires&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T23:20:39-07:00","id":974904,"title":"","content":"the Syndicate does this all the time, this is the basis of their concept. They find something the Vampire, or werewolf or whatever wants that is less costly than going head to head against whatever they send them after. Hell some do that with Tradition mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T00:48:57-07:00","id":974929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=974768#post974768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the effect is applied with their permission, or the vampire doesn't have the above means at hand, it's not going to spontaneously stop just because &quot;lol vampires&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't realize the gravity of the situation. We're not talking about messing with a vampire, we're talking about messing with the curse.<br /> Affecting the curse is difficult (if not impossible) and vulgar, and it gets worse with lower gens.<br /> <br /> Assuming it even works. That would only be possible with weak bloods (14th/15th gen and dhampirs).<br /> For anyone else, the changes will fade on the next sunrise...assuming the guy survived the backlash.<br /> <br /> No matter the game you run, that sort of mechanics shouldn't even be considered (even demonic Investments involved)...it's the ultimate power gaming mechanic.<br /> If vampires could counter their curses so easily, we have a big problem...a very big one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=974718#post974718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, to put it another way, I'm advocating the Union mind whack their hemophage agent to never kill unless either ordered to by a superior, or as a matter of self defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to go this route, just consider Honorable Accord. It's trouble, but it has more chances of succeeding than humanity.<br /> <br /> Humanity in the Technocracy?...don't make me laugh.<br /> &quot;I don't have to kill so my humanity is fine...&quot; that never works. Simply witnessing what Technos do would trigger degeneration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-23-2016, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T02:16:47-07:00","id":974948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=974929#post974929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity in the Technocracy?...don't make me laugh.<br /> &quot;I don't have to kill so my humanity is fine...&quot; that never works. Simply witnessing what Technos do would trigger degeneration.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not how the Technocracy works Pleiades. The Technocracy is a fundamentally human organization and we have plenty of canon examples of Technocratic agents acting plenty human, such as the Syndicate Agent that has to shut down a Progenitor facility that attempts to make a cure for cancer, because the Masses wouldn't acccept it. Then she goes to a bar and talks to the bartender about how shit she feels and how she doesn't like doing this, at the end of it she mindwipes him, because she can't just give classified information away, but she transfers a million dollars to him as gratitude for having someone to talk to. <br /> <br /> This is the Syndicate mind you, the Convention most often stereotyped to be capitalists with no regrets who'd sell out their mothers to turn in a profit.<br /> <br /> Likewise, we have people like the Progenitors in Applied Science who go out there on the frontlines and use the fact that they're transhuman badasses for something other than university politics and actually fight monsters (they also kill faith healers and people who use homeopathy because they want to help sleepers, and faith healing/homeopathy won't actually work when the dude that does it isn't there.)<br /> <br /> Calling the Technocratic Union inhuman and eeeeeeevil is a really easy trap to fall into, but it ultimately diminishes the horror of the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Because, ultimately the Union is an organization founded, led, staffed and served by human men and women, fighting for what they believe in.<br /> <br /> There is something about eggs and omelets that goes unsaid in that sentence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T02:51:36-07:00","id":974959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=974948#post974948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calling the Technocratic Union inhuman and eeeeeeevil is a really easy trap to fall into, but it ultimately diminishes the horror of the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about evil, since vampires are evil by nature. And I'm not talking about technocracy, I'm talking about vampires in technocracy.<br /> <br /> The matter has been discussed many times in the forums and the books. Transhumanism, fighting monsters, killing the &quot;bad guys&quot;, toying with magic and disciplines. All of these, while not inherently evil are bad for humanity.<br /> &quot;I'm doing this for the good of mankind&quot; isn't a viable excuse. The beast will take the opportunity and wreck you (that's the central point in VtM).<br /> <br /> That's why the Tzimisce, the evil transhumanist fascist fanatic ego-maniacs and all Vampires that follow their doctrines are almost all on Paths.<br /> Even those that keep a nice attitude can't hold on to humanity and eventually subscribe to Honorable Accord.<br /> <br /> A vampire working for the syndicate may have a rating of 4-5.<br /> A vampire who plays around with progenitors, It-X and the like can't hope to have more than 3 (and even that is very optimistic). Not because it's evil, but because it's inhuman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-23-2016, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T06:20:07-07:00","id":975019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=974959#post974959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not talking about evil, since vampires are evil by nature. And I'm not talking about technocracy, I'm talking about vampires in technocracy.<br /> <br /> The matter has been discussed many times in the forums and the books. Transhumanism, fighting monsters, killing the &quot;bad guys&quot;, toying with magic and disciplines. All of these, while not inherently evil are bad for humanity.<br /> &quot;I'm doing this for the good of mankind&quot; isn't a viable excuse. The beast will take the opportunity and wreck you (that's the central point in VtM).<br /> <br /> That's why the Tzimisce, the evil transhumanist fascist fanatic ego-maniacs and all Vampires that follow their doctrines are almost all on Paths.<br /> Even those that keep a nice attitude can't hold on to humanity and eventually subscribe to Honorable Accord.<br /> <br /> A vampire working for the syndicate may have a rating of 4-5.<br /> A vampire who plays around with progenitors, It-X and the like can't hope to have more than 3 (and even that is very optimistic). Not because it's evil, but because it's inhuman.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not the case. Currently It-X and progenitors are among the most humane of the Conventions - especially the Progenitors. Our altruistic bleeding-heart Progs are almost as &quot;good&quot; and &quot;humane&quot; as the Void Engineers. And very, very ethical. So-called doctors of the Union's ethics, moral compass, humanity and compassion are all recurring theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 09-23-2016, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T07:45:57-07:00","id":975045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975019#post975019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not the case. Currently It-X and progenitors are among the most humane of the Conventions - especially the Progenitors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said inhuman not &quot;inhumane&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T08:53:20-07:00","id":975078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975019#post975019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our altruistic bleeding-heart Progs are almost as &quot;good&quot; and &quot;humane&quot; as the Void Engineers. And very, very ethical. So-called doctors of the Union's ethics, moral compass, humanity and compassion are all recurring theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for all the eugenics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T09:08:07-07:00","id":975086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975078#post975078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for all the eugenics.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have none. Long time ago, they purged it from their system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T09:12:29-07:00","id":975088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975086#post975086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have none. Long time ago, they purged it from their system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh-huh. Sure they did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T10:42:33-07:00","id":975120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=974929#post974929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't realize the gravity of the situation. We're not talking about messing with a vampire, we're talking about messing with the curse.<br /> Affecting the curse is difficult (if not impossible) and vulgar, and it gets worse with lower gens.<br /> <br /> Assuming it even works. That would only be possible with weak bloods (14th/15th gen and dhampirs).<br /> For anyone else, the changes will fade on the next sunrise...assuming the guy survived the backlash.<br /> <br /> No matter the game you run, that sort of mechanics shouldn't even be considered (even demonic Investments involved)...it's the ultimate power gaming mechanic.<br /> If vampires could counter their curses so easily, we have a big problem...a very big one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize the gravity of the situation just fine, thank you very much. Most of my solutions apart from the &quot;basically rewrite their mind entirely to not have the Beast&quot; were tailored to very specifically <i>not</i> go up against the Curse of Caine. Bluecho's likewise meets that criterion.<br /> <br /> Vampires in Frenzy can be Dominated. It's harder than when they aren't in Frenzy, but it's a thing. Implanting compulsions in a vampire is likewise a thing, as evidenced by Dominate having such an ability. This means that mind-control of those particular natures are specifically <i>not</i> incompatible with the Curse.<br /> <br /> Having different difficulties for your Virtue rolls is a bunch of Merits that you can just take as a vampire. Again, compatible on some level with the Curse. It's just buffing something the vampire can already do as part of their condition.<br /> <br /> Restoring Humanity accelerates something vampires can already do. You can regain Humanity, mechanically with XP expenditure and in-character with various means of restoring your moral core. Same with Paths. It <i>would</i> probably be Vulgar outside a Sanctum, in parallel to how Verbena Revised treats permanently improving Attributes.<br /> <br /> Not one of these options require actually opposing the Curse on the Mage's part. They each involve affecting the vampire's own innate <i>defenses</i> against the Beast - their Virtues or their Humanity - or controlling them via means that already demonstrably work against frenzied vampires.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The only one that you <i>might</i> have something resembling a point against is the total rewrite suggestion... which as I mentioned requires <i>at the very least</i> Mind 5, and I'd also say a whole lot of successes. Adding &quot;is universally vulgar everywhere, yes even there&quot; is just layering shit topping on the shit sandwich the method already is.<br /> <br /> It might actually be <i>easier</i> to just transfer the vampire's mind to a blank clone, destroy the original body, and then fix them up there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T10:43:26-07:00","id":975121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975088#post975088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh-huh. Sure they did.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You made a claim and I'd like to see you prove it.<br /> <br /> Though I will not deny that they totally did support it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T10:45:13-07:00","id":975122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975086#post975086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have none. Long time ago, they purged it from their system.</div> </div> </div> </div>They sort of do. The current genetic engineering movement in the Progenitors can be somewhat tied to their original eugenics ideas, it's just a more modernly-acceptable method.<br /> <br /> They <i>are</i> considerably better now that all the Wicked Old (mostly) Men out in space were removed, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T12:30:11-07:00","id":975168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975122#post975122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They sort of do. The current genetic engineering movement in the Progenitors can be somewhat tied to their original eugenics ideas, it's just a more modernly-acceptable method.<br /> <br /> They <i>are</i> considerably better now that all the Wicked Old (mostly) Men out in space were removed, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, the Conventions in general became waaaaay more humanitarian when they lost the Inner Circle and Control.<br /> <br /> And then there's the Void Engineers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T12:33:27-07:00","id":975170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975120#post975120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not one of these options require actually opposing the Curse on the Mage's part. They each involve affecting the vampire's own innate <i>defenses</i> against the Beast - their Virtues or their Humanity - or controlling them via means that already demonstrably work against frenzied vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm getting confused...I can't agree with you here...okay, I'll use the equivalence:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>In the first case:</b> compulsion, domination, doesn't affect the vampire's innate defenses. you override the vampire's will with your own. If the override is powerful enough, even the beast can't resist it.<br /> In a way, you're taking the vampire's place in challenging the beast...<br /> <br /> <b>The second case:</b> improving virtue rolls. The only equivalent I found for it is Dementation (and Daimonion, but that's a special case). I still don't know how Dementation works, but it's closer to your objective of affecting the vampire's own innate defenses.<br /> <br /> <b>The third case:</b> merits. they &quot;are&quot; related to the curse.<br /> Let's say, these specific merits/flaws as well as clan weaknesses and similar effects are simply a configuration of the curse. They cannot be manipulated, and they cannot be induced (of course, unless you score 10+ successes...).<br /> <br /> To get back to the first 2 cases:<br /> <br /> Compulsion, Domination (or equivalent), assuming there's a way to make it permanent and force your will permanently, the vampire's own will would have to be broken...yes the beast is less likely to resist the compulsion, but the vampire is also less likely to resist the beast, which kinda defeats the original purpose. You're not improving the vampire's defenses, you're destroying them.<br /> <br /> The Dementation equivalent is countered by humanity/path rating. For the effect to be permanent, the vampire would have to have a low morality rating (which means, more sensitive to the beast) which, again, defeats the original purpose.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-23-2016, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T15:28:02-07:00","id":975252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975170#post975170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>In the first case:</b> compulsion, domination, doesn't affect the vampire's innate defenses. you override the vampire's will with your own. If the override is powerful enough, even the beast can't resist it.<br /> In a way, you're taking the vampire's place in challenging the beast...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just mind control. Mind controlling the Beast isn't some great and powerful incomprehensibility, it's just hard. They're still in frenzy, so no portion of the Curse itself is being negated or opposed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The second case:</b> improving virtue rolls. The only equivalent I found for it is Dementation (and Daimonion, but that's a special case). I still don't know how Dementation works, but it's closer to your objective of affecting the vampire's own innate defenses.<br /> <br /> <b>The third case:</b> merits. they &quot;are&quot; related to the curse.<br /> Let's say, these specific merits/flaws as well as clan weaknesses and similar effects are simply a configuration of the curse. They cannot be manipulated, and they cannot be induced (of course, unless you score 10+ successes...). </div> </div> </div>Those are both the same case.<br /> <br /> Merits that reduce the relevant difficulties:<br /> <b>King or Queen of Shadow, Lore of the Clans p. 122.</b> &quot;It is hard to hold onto your Humanity within the Sabbat, or even simply as a vampire. However, you draw strength from your ability to empathize with the kine. Any degeneration checks you make while on Path of Humanity reduce their difficulty by two.&quot; I'm fairly sure that the Curse doesn't <i>help</i> you empathize with mortals.<br /> <b>Impressive Restraint, Lore of the Clans p. 200.</b> &quot;When you haven\u2019t fed, it can be torturous to be near mortals. The pounding thrum of blood through their veins does not leave you nearly as tempted as it might other Kindred. When opportunity presents itself, the difficulty of all Self-Control rolls to resist hunger are made against a -2 difficulty. Characters on Paths of Enlightenment that require Instinct cannot take this Merit.&quot;<br /> <b>Philosophical Humanist, Road of Humanity p. 73.</b> &quot;You do not much care as to whether or not the Biblical Cain was the forefather of all vampires, whether he was cursed by God or, indeed, if God or Caine even exist. Nor do you buy into the superstitious folderol surrounding the Beast. It is, to you, neither a demon nor some \u201cevil self\u201d; it is simply a manifestation of normal, if dark, human passions, passions exacerbated by the transformative power of the Embrace.<br /> As a result, you find yourself at an advantage in combating the Beast through the judicious application of reason. All of your rolls to resist frenzy and R\u00f6tshreck are at a \u20131 difficulty. Brujah Cainites, though no less capable than any other clan of waxing secular regarding the Curse (and often more inclined to do so), may not take this Merit.&quot;<br /> <b>Controlled Thirst, Player's Guide to the High Clans, p. 203.</b> &quot;Regular time spent among mortals has dulled the hungers of your palette. You reduce the difficulty of any frenzy roll involving the sight, scent or taste of blood by one. You cannot frenzy from sensing blood if your blood pool is full; conversely, you lose your normal difficulty reduction if your blood pool is less than a quarter full (rounded down).&quot;<br /> <br /> There are also merits that give you extra dice for these purposes:<br /> <b>Calm Heart, V20 p. 485.</b> &quot;You are naturally calm and do not easily fly off the handle. You receive two extra dice when attempting to resist a frenzy. Brujah may not take this Merit.&quot;<br /> <b>Slowed Degeneration, Lore of the Clans p. 200.</b> &quot;Your Humanity is strong and can more easily withstand the Beast\u2019s assaults. You gain two additional dice on any Conscience roll. This degree of moral resilience allows a well-behaved vampire to lose Humanity at a much slower rate than would otherwise be possible. Only vampires following Humanity may take this Merit, and the Merit is lost forever in the event that the vampire takes up another Path of Enlightenment.&quot;<br /> <b>Lion-Hearted, Player's Guide to the High Clans, p. 204.</b> &quot;In a moment of great crisis, you may call upon your honor and nobility to fortify your resolve. Once per story, you may spend a point of Willpower to substitute your Road rating for both your Self-Control/Conviction and Courage for the scene. Characters who ascribe to roads that do not venerate heroism and valor may not purchase or retain this Merit, particularly those on the Road of Sin (although followers of the Via Adversarius may possess this Merit; see Road of Sin for more information).&quot;<br /> <b>Flock, Player's Guide to the Low Clans, p. 186.</b> &quot;You feel strong ties of kinship with a specific community of mortals. The difficulty to resist frenzy is always two less than normal where your flock is concerned, enabling you to better withstand the lure of their blood and forgive their trespasses. If you do succumb to frenzy, you may spend one Willpower point to recognize members of your flock as friends. As long as these individuals stay out of your way and do not directly provoke you, you may ignore them for the duration of the rampage. This Merit is often coupled with the Prey Exclusion Flaw (Dark Ages: Vampire p. 305). Storytellers should feel free to disallow any communities deemed unbalancing or too inclusive.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, which of those are you claiming are 'permutations of the Curse' rather than aspects of the vampire's personality or circumstance? And on what basis?<br /> <br /> If a vampire had Eidetic Memory when they were a mortal, and then were Embraced, is that now a permutation of the Curse?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To get back to the first 2 cases:<br /> <br /> Compulsion, Domination (or equivalent), assuming there's a way to make it permanent and force your will permanently, the vampire's own will would have to be broken...yes the beast is less likely to resist the compulsion, but the vampire is also less likely to resist the beast, which kinda defeats the original purpose. You're not improving the vampire's defenses, you're destroying them. </div> </div> </div>See Dominate 4, V20 pp. 154-155. Or Technocratic Conditioning. Worst-case, you need to deplete their temporary Willpower, which at most means they can't spend Willpower to negate frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-23-2016, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T16:16:44-07:00","id":975264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975170#post975170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unless you score 10+ successes...).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll just note that since magic is an extended roll, this isn't actually a <i>problem</i> when you have them contained in a Technocratic lab.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T02:10:27-07:00","id":975435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975264#post975264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll just note that since magic is an extended roll, this isn't actually a <i>problem</i> when you have them contained in a Technocratic lab.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, mages make extended rolls, so does God...and God doesn't need a lab.<br /> <br /> Just kidding...the process is difficult and vulgar, with the chance of fading after sunrise and blah blah blah.<br /> <br /> I've already said that in my previous posts. I'd prefer if I didn't have to repeat myself, and arguing for the sake of arguing gets old very quickly (but I guess, that's the charm of Mage forums...).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975252#post975252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just mind control. Mind controlling the Beast isn't some great and powerful incomprehensibility, it's just hard. They're still in frenzy, so no portion of the Curse itself is being negated or opposed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I wasn't addressing the curse in that particular portion, just saying that it didn't improve the vampire's innate defenses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975252#post975252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are both the same case.</div> </div> </div> </div>nope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975252#post975252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, which of those are you claiming are 'permutations of the Curse' rather than aspects of the vampire's personality or circumstance? And on what basis?If a vampire had Eidetic Memory when they were a mortal, and then were Embraced, is that now a permutation of the Curse?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you take a merit/flaw that supposedly counters the curse, it's not that the curse is countered, just that the curse is weaker in your case.<br /> <br /> Now, I admit that the concept was thrown out the window in some editions (v20 and DA) and the game was broken, because both editions made it so Humanity was actually a thing (while Revised had Humanity as a lie). Still, the authors in DA encouraged discretion when using the merits (because they were definitely broken).<br /> <br /> Anyway, in this case, we don't talk about the Curse, because there is none. V20 (and to some extent DA) basically allows you to create vampires without curse or banes (no stasis, countered clan weaknesses, you could even have your beast ignored or downright removed etc...).<br /> <br /> In this case, it's not that the curse is countered, it's just that the curse is not a curse anymore. Like I said in my previous posts, vampires with weak or absent curses (14th/15th gen and dhampirs) could easily be manipulated by mages. And a vampire with too many merits (weak curse) would be as easy to manipulate as a weak blood. So, at least, no arguing there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975252#post975252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See Dominate 4, V20 pp. 154-155. Or Technocratic Conditioning. Worst-case, you need to deplete their temporary Willpower, which at most means they can't spend Willpower to negate frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conditioning does not affect the beast. You still have to give commands (which are resisted with willpower and a botch just renders them immune to the commands).<br /> <br /> Weak willed, weak minded conditioned vampires are less likely to resist the beast (as if it needed to be said), not only because they can't spend willpower, but because they're weak mindless husks with no proper self control (assuming they had any, prior to the conditioning).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-24-2016, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T02:58:35-07:00","id":975448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975435#post975435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, mages make extended rolls, so does God...and God doesn't need a lab.<br /> <br /> Just kidding...the process is difficult and vulgar, with the chance of fading after sunrise and blah blah blah.<br /> <br /> I've already said that in my previous posts. I'd prefer if I didn't have to repeat myself, and arguing for the sake of arguing gets old very quickly (but I guess, that's the charm of Mage forums...).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I will gladly admit that as a Mage fan, I despise arguing over a lot of these things, I tend to run with &quot;do what you want to do at your table&quot;.<br /> <br /> I took a look at M20 and decided that to me, the way to do this would be Mind 4, Prime 2 working that required 10 successes and might fade with sunrise if it is not reinforced with Conditioning. It will be ridiculously vulgar if not performed outside of a dedicated lab (Sanctum), and Paradox Backlashes would take the form of accidentally providing backdoors for the Beast so it screws you up later. The Mind 4 is there due to mind control, and the Prime 2 is there to give it a power source and make it self-reinforcing.<br /> <br /> This is how I'd do it at my table anyways, I can't really see why the Technocracy would <i>want</i> vampires anyway, but whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T03:16:36-07:00","id":975454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975448#post975448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is how I'd do it at my table anyways, I can't really see why the Technocracy would <i>want</i> vampires anyway, but whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually just assume it's as dangerous and rewarding as a vampire conditioning a Lupine.<br /> A vampire gets a powerful, immune to sunlight with delirium retainers. But runs the risk of having a mad dog tearing them apart or screwing their domain.<br /> <br /> A mage could benefit from a relatively powerful, immune to paradox vampire agent. But they'd have to choose between a beast ridden husk or an inhuman fanatic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T05:15:36-07:00","id":975476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975435#post975435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I wasn't addressing the curse in that particular portion, just saying that it didn't improve the vampire's innate defenses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh.<br /> <br /> Sure. That's accurate.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> nope. </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975120#post975120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having different difficulties for your <b>Virtue rolls</b> is a bunch of <b>Merits</b> that you can just take as a vampire. Again, compatible on some level with the Curse. It's just buffing something the vampire can already do as part of their condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oi. Quit moving the damn goalposts. The argument is that <i>because there are Merits which are not reflections of the Curse, but of the person</i>, then <i>affecting the person rather than the Curse is possible</i>, and since <i>those self-same Merits modify Virtue rolls</i>, that <i>you can modify Virtue rolls without interacting with the Curse itself</i>. And thus not Always Vulgar Under Every Circumstance.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you take a merit/flaw that supposedly counters the curse, it's not that the curse is countered, just that the curse is weaker in your case.<br /> <br /> Now, I admit that the concept was thrown out the window in some editions (v20 and DA) and the game was broken, because both editions made it so Humanity was actually a thing (while Revised had Humanity as a lie). Still, the authors in DA encouraged discretion when using the merits (because they were definitely broken). </div> </div> </div>...um, what? I'm... not entirely sure what you're trying to say here.<br /> <br /> Are you saying that all of the merits in question aren't strengthening the Man, but rather weakening the Beast? I.e., that they don't represent better self-discipline on the vampire's part at all but the Curse of Caine itself being weaker in them?<br /> <br /> That seems weird to me. If that is what you're saying... yeah you naturally wouldn't agree with any of the proposed ideas. Not... really much to be discussed there.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, in this case, we don't talk about the Curse, because there is none. V20 (and to some extent DA) basically allows you to create vampires without curse or banes (no stasis, countered clan weaknesses, you could even have your beast ignored or downright removed etc...).<br /> <br /> In this case, it's not that the curse is countered, it's just that the curse is not a curse anymore. Like I said in my previous posts, vampires with weak or absent curses (14th/15th gen and dhampirs) could easily be manipulated by mages. And a vampire with too many merits (weak curse) would be as easy to manipulate as a weak blood. So, at least, no arguing there. </div> </div> </div>I've always been under the impression that aside from Golconda and Final Death, none of that stuff <i>removes</i> the Curse of Caine.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Conditioning does not affect the beast. You still have to give commands (which are resisted with willpower and a botch just renders them immune to the commands).<br /> <br /> Weak willed, weak minded conditioned vampires are less likely to resist the beast (as if it needed to be said), not only because they can't spend willpower, but because they're weak mindless husks with no proper self control (assuming they had any, prior to the conditioning). </div> </div> </div>The Conditioning is for Bluecho's suggestion that deep-level programming be put in which prohibits committing the sorts of acts ('utter depravity', feeding beyond satiation, etc.) which result in Humanity degradation below the Humanity 3 level. That doesn't require applying it to the Beast, so I'm not sure how this is relevant.<br /> <br /> The bit about leaving them an empty husk less able to resist the Beast is interesting, if true. However, I can't find anything in Dominate about it. That's also not how Technocratic Conditioning, which is quite a bit less severe than Dominate 4, works. Where is this from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-24-2016, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T06:26:10-07:00","id":975488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975476#post975476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oi. Quit moving the damn goalposts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's asking too much, I'm having a hard time keeping all the details in sync.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975476#post975476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you saying that all of the merits in question aren't strengthening the Man, but rather weakening the Beast? I.e., that they don't represent better self-discipline on the vampire's part at all but the Curse of Caine itself being weaker in them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've always been under the impression that aside from Golconda and Final Death, none of that stuff <i>removes</i> the Curse of Caine. </div> </div> </div>When you reach the point where the sun is the only thing that troubles you in any meaningful way, it's hardly a curse anymore, it's more like...Heliophobia or some extreme case of albinism.<br /> <br /> Getting immortality and power without having to pay a significant price is not a curse, it's a blessing. Even Golconda has its price.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975476#post975476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't require applying it to the Beast, so I'm not sure how this is relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most vampires don't want to commit such atrocities or don't bother committing them (unless their morality dictates it). It's usually the beast that commits them, and the vampire is still responsible for the beast's actions...or bad luck.<br /> <br /> So Bluecho's solution is a bit redundant if it cannot be applied to the beast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975476#post975476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> However, I can't find anything in Dominate about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, there is no detailed list of &quot;how the beast works in what situation&quot; (it would be a huge list). We just have pointers for the ST to handle (that's why there's so many threads about it in VtM forums).<br /> <br /> Anyway, In the case of the conditioned husk, it's quite simple. The victim loses much of their individuality and sense of self. They have no initiative and notions of self control weaken.<br /> Such a weakness is an easy gateway for the beast. The victim is less capable of denying the beast's rage, assuming they care at all (the weakest would just let the beast do whatever it wants). Add to that the fact that the beast gets more frustrated from the lack of indulgence...<br /> <br /> mechanically, this would manifest as either a higher difficulty to resist, a loss of dice to resist or a derangement describing the husk like state (again with penalties).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-24-2016, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T08:38:33-07:00","id":975533,"title":"","content":"The Beast is a manifestation of the dark urges of the Kindred, it is more similar to the Rage of the Garou than the P'o of the Kuei-jin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T11:02:34-07:00","id":975606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975533#post975533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beast is a manifestation of the dark urges of the Kindred, it is more similar to the Rage of the Garou than the P'o of the Kuei-jin.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's both and neither...something between the two. It's not a split soul or an inner urge, it's a split urge from cursed blood.<br /> <br /> Self-Control gives the Rage perspective: inner urges to be suppressed.<br /> <br /> Instinct gives the P'o perspective: a separate entity to be controlled.<br /> <br /> Both perspectives seem to have some right and some wrong...Well, until the authors decide to give us a clear answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T15:38:04-07:00","id":976126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=975488#post975488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guess that's that then. I can't agree. It takes too much of the vampire's own actions - and the responsibility for their own damnation - away from them. And seems to willfully disregard all the text that isn't raw mechanics.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most vampires don't want to commit such atrocities or don't bother committing them (unless their morality dictates it). It's usually the beast that commits them, and the vampire is still responsible for the beast's actions...or bad luck.<br /> <br /> So Bluecho's solution is a bit redundant if it cannot be applied to the beast. </div> </div> </div>Most vampires are also at higher than Humanity 3. And &quot;redundant&quot; means something <i>very different</i> when you're talking about things like this - it means <i>resilient</i>, not wasteful.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unfortunately, there is no detailed list of &quot;how the beast works in what situation&quot; (it would be a huge list). We just have pointers for the ST to handle (that's why there's so many threads about it in VtM forums).<br /> <br /> Anyway, In the case of the conditioned husk, it's quite simple. The victim loses much of their individuality and sense of self. They have no initiative and notions of self control weaken.<br /> Such a weakness is an easy gateway for the beast. The victim is less capable of denying the beast's rage, assuming they care at all (the weakest would just let the beast do whatever it wants). Add to that the fact that the beast gets more frustrated from the lack of indulgence...<br /> <br /> mechanically, this would manifest as either a higher difficulty to resist, a loss of dice to resist or a derangement describing the husk like state (again with penalties). </div> </div> </div>Okay, but basically all of this is a housrule. It's not &quot;this is how it works&quot; but &quot;this is how Pleiades <i>wants</i> it to work&quot;.<br /> <br /> Moreover, people with Conditioning have a sense of self. They have individuality. It takes a great effort of will to act against it, but that's will that they <i>have</i>. Calling them an &quot;empty husk&quot; is hyperbole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-25-2016, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T16:18:06-07:00","id":976146,"title":"","content":"This is, incidentally also the reason why the Technocracy <i>uses</i> Conditioning, because a Mage that cannot think for themselves is <i>fucking useless</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T17:56:07-07:00","id":976195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=976126#post976126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most vampires are also at higher than Humanity 3. And &quot;redundant&quot; means something <i>very different</i> when you're talking about things like this - it means <i>resilient</i>, not wasteful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Redundancy isn't a bug, it's a <i>feature</i>. Especially when it keeps a blood-drinking parasite from going off the moral event horizon and becoming a mindless animal. So far as the Union is concerned - and it's the Union that decides whether Conditioning is used on one of their assets, not the asset themselves - the added protection is well worth the effort installing it.<br /> <br /> And yes, Conditioning doesn't necessarily result in the subject becoming a hollowed out husk. There are ten entire levels of Conditioning, and only the highest could be considered as turning the subject into a drone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T23:39:20-07:00","id":976393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=976195#post976195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. Redundancy isn't a bug, it's a <i>feature</i>. Especially when it keeps a blood-drinking parasite from going off the moral event horizon and becoming a mindless animal. So far as the Union is concerned - and it's the Union that decides whether Conditioning is used on one of their assets, not the asset themselves - the added protection is well worth the effort installing it.<br /> <br /> And yes, Conditioning doesn't necessarily result in the subject becoming a hollowed out husk. There are ten entire levels of Conditioning, and only the highest could be considered as turning the subject into a drone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And even then, the description of Conditioning 10, is simply &quot;he had learned to love Big Brother.&quot;<br /> <br /> Winston in 1984 isn't a thoughtless drone, he's just <i>reaaaally </i>traumatized and broken inside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T03:54:33-07:00","id":976453,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=976146#post976146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is, incidentally also the reason why the Technocracy <i>uses</i> Conditioning, because a Mage that cannot think for themselves is <i>fucking useless</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are you still talking about mages? they don't have beasts to deal with, and they keep their mortal feelings.<br /> <br /> The standard techno has a humanity 3. And a planned violation is lvl 3 sin...meaning a vampire techno would be on lvl 2-3...which is not very stable. Or as described in the books, the vampire either has no self-control or no conscience (which is bad either way).<br /> Conditioning will only worsen the case. That's why the technique is favored by Sabbat with dominate, makes it harder to resist the urge and easier to shatter morality until the victim can't distinguish right from wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=976126#post976126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, people with Conditioning have a sense of self. They have individuality. It takes a great effort of will to act against it, but that's will that they <i>have</i>. Calling them an &quot;empty husk&quot; is hyperbole.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Yet vampires must pay a high price for<br /> the minds they ensnare. Servants Dominated in this<br /> way lose much of their passion and individuality. They<br /> follow the vampire\u2019s orders quite literally, seldom taking<br /> initiative or showing any imagination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=976126#post976126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess that's that then. I can't agree. It takes too much of the vampire's own actions - and the responsibility for their own damnation - away from them. And seems to willfully disregard all the text that isn't raw mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the tragedy of vampiric existence. Welcome to personal-horror. If they don't like it, the sun is here, working 15 hours a day to release them if they want.<br /> Or they can try maintaining their humanity and reach Golconda through isolation...that means no Jyhad, no Ascension war, no technocracy etc...<br /> <br /> Otherwise, they take the responsibility for their actions and those of their beast. If you want to undermine that central aspect of VtM, feel free to do so. But don't pretend I'm the own doing the houseruling.<br /> <br /> The best one can hope from magic is the Red Sign ritual...which makes you turn back into a human (not what we're looking for...).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=976126#post976126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but basically all of this is a housrule. It's not &quot;this is how it works&quot; but &quot;this is how Pleiades <i>wants</i> it to work&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not houseruling, just illustrating through mechanics what is usually handled through roleplaying.<br /> <br /> My reasoning comes from several books that treat the subject of morality and beast (the most detailed being Chaining the Beast (2003), but several books have their own pointers) as well as mental states an several stories portraying situations where the character will face Frenzy or downright degeneration...and trust me, simply &quot;witnessing&quot; (not even doing) a Progenitor dissecting a vampire, an Iterator having his head torn by a zulo or a blood feast can cause degeneration. Simply having a group of people staring at you the wrong way can cause Frenzy...<br /> <br /> So, if anything, you're the one Houseruling by saying the beast can be countered by a simple wave of a wand, which is the same as saying a HIT Mark can become a vampire thanks to a de-intoxicating ritae.<br /> <br /> The only advantage of conditioning is that the conditioner will have less impact on the slave's psyche, which means the vampire is less likely to frenzy on Big-Brother (if ever), but his weak-mindedness will make him less likely or capable of resisting the beast when in the field...otherwise, shovelheads would be much easier to keep in line.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-26-2016, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T06:37:25-07:00","id":976495,"title":"","content":"...Are you using the Dominate ability named Conditioning, or the one presented in Guide to The Technocracy, because the closest to what you're describing, is the Procedure used to make <i>fucking ATLAS Units</i>, which is basically a hypercharged version of the normal Conditioning. Most normal humans have some degree of Conditioning, because growing up in the system created by the Technocracy leaves you slightly Conditioned.<br /> <br /> The Dominate Conditioning is not Technocrat Conditioning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T07:08:16-07:00","id":976504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=976495#post976495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dominate Conditioning is not Technocrat Conditioning.</div> </div> </div> </div>We were discussing implanting compulsions in the way Dominate does (conditioning for permanent effect).<br /> I doubt the regular technocracy conditioning could do that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T07:48:42-07:00","id":976517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=976504#post976504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We were discussing implanting compulsions in the way Dominate does (conditioning for permanent effect).<br /> I doubt the regular technocracy conditioning could do that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's actually the primary purpose of it, now that you mention it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T07:58:30-07:00","id":976520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=976517#post976517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually the primary purpose of it, now that you mention it.</div> </div> </div> </div>what, making Atlas units? you just said making Atlas units was a hypercharged version of the normal conditioning...which is what dominate conditioning is (hypercharged version).<br /> <br /> EDIT: did I misunderstand something? or did I poorly express myself? 'cause English is not my native language.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-26-2016, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T08:12:53-07:00","id":976526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=976520#post976520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> what, making Atlas units? you just said making Atlas units was a hypercharged version of the normal conditioning (like in dominate conditioning).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, I may be the problem here due to unclearness.<br /> <br /> Technocratic Conditioning works like this:<br /> <br /> Conditioning goes from a scale of 1 to 10, where each rank adds a new nasty thing that your superiors can make you do. It looks kinda like this:<br /> <br /> <b>1</b>: Will forego food and sleep if necessary to carry out the mission. Reality Deviants see a Technocratic version of their Ascension.<br /> <b>2</b>: Will submit to most minor Technocratic Procedures without resistance.<br /> <b>3</b>: Can be ordered to see an individual as an ally or enemy, as ordered by Control. A Reality Deviant will refuse to use minor Traditionalist Procedures if they require a non-Technocratic Focus.<br /> <b>4</b>: Is installed with a code word that causes the character to see another person as &quot;unmutual&quot;, whom he will avoid and ostracize at any point until reversed.<br /> <b>5</b>: Is installed with a code word that causes the character to become docile and pacifistic. A Reality Deviant will use a Technocratic Focus for one of his Spheres.<br /> <b>6</b>: Is installed with a code word that causes the character to enact an elaborate scheme against a chosen individual.<br /> <b>7</b>: Is implanted with the idea that a certain group of individuals is an ally that must be trusted. A Reality Deviant has all of his Foci replaced with Technocratic Foci.<br /> <b>8</b>: The subject can now be ordered to completely forget a specific individual.<br /> <b>9</b>: The subject will betray any individual no matter how loved, if ordered to by Control.<br /> <b>10</b>: The subject will treat a specific person, ideal or organization with almost religious devotion. Blah blah blah, resistanc is futile blah blah big brother.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, what the Technocracy uses to make ATLAS units is called Processing, and requires the subject to be Conditioned.<br /> <br /> <b>Processing (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Mind, \u2022\u2022 Prime)</b><br /> With Social Conditioning and Programming (see Guide to the Technocracy), the Technocracy manipulates proles and agents to be completely loyal. Indoctrination<br /> takes a Reality Deviant and bends him to the Union\u2019s will. The Procedure itself is not for the faint of heart. It used to require loud music, straps, holographic projectors, acupuncture needles, bad food, and a dentist\u2019s chair \u2014 not necessarily in that order \u2014 and all over the course of one hellish week.<br /> <br /> Today, the NWO finds it more efficient to disconnect a target\u2019s senses from his nervous system (usually through forcible installation of a DNI) before employing many, many sessions of interrogation and personality correction. No small number of agents have walked out during field training because of Processing. Members of the Feed have gone so far as to lobby for its removal from standard protocol. The Ivory Tower\u2019s counterargument has been \u201cvictory by any means necessary,\u201d and the Operatives use it extensively for their Enlightened Shock Corps experiment. What happens when you strap a mage down and make him wish for death?<br /> <br /> With this Procedure, eventually, you remove his identity. He\u2019s left ready to be rebuilt in the Technocracy\u2019s image. But this rebuilding is not painted over a blank slate; it\u2019s painted over countless scars, resulting in an imperfect creation. This adds to the tragedy, as such newly indoctrinated agents are treated as disposable assets. <br /> <br /> Some rise to greatness, but this throwaway treatment, along with the emotional trauma of the Procedure, lead to daunting suicide rates. These rates are even higher if one considers the number of new agents who die in a hail of fire from their former allies, ending them out of mercy.<br /> <br /> This is cruelly referred to as \u201csuicide by Reality Deviant.\u201d The Procedure is never truly complete. The indoctrinated agent becomes a Technocrat, for all intents and purposes. However, in a time of massive stress, the player can spend a point of Willpower for his character to briefly snap back to his original identity for one turn.But because of the reprogramming, he\u2019s unable to act against the Union. This often results in self-destructive behavior. Due of this, such assets are routinely re-Processed to ensure continued service<br /> _<br /> <br /> I hope this helped. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T08:30:00-07:00","id":976538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=976526#post976526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Processing (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Mind, \u2022\u2022 Prime)</b><br /> <br /> I hope this helped. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this. It's much similar to dominate conditioning and sabbat indoctrination methods.<br /> <br /> The remaining problem is how the beast reacts to this state. My position is that the victim is less capable of resisting the beast's urges (that are separate from the victim's). A result of their &quot;loss of identity&quot; and &quot;self-destructive behavior&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-26-2016, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T11:04:47-07:00","id":976616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=976538#post976538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, this. It's much similar to dominate conditioning and sabbat indoctrination methods.<br /> <br /> The remaining problem is how the beast reacts to this state. My position is that the victim is less capable of resisting the beast's urges (that are separate from the victim's). A result of their &quot;loss of identity&quot; and &quot;self-destructive behavior&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm inclined to agree that if you use actual Processing on a vampire, then my response would be &quot;get rekt scrub&quot; and totally note that it makes them incapable of effectively resisting the Beast, because where there used to be a wall to protect against it, there is now <i>a giant fucking hole</i>.<br /> <br /> As a Storyteller, I'd be much more sadistic and go like &quot;thank you, you've taught the Beast to be smart.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T19:45:31-07:00","id":976894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=976453#post976453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the tragedy of vampiric existence. Welcome to personal-horror. If they don't like it, the sun is here, working 15 hours a day to release them if they want.<br /> Or they can try maintaining their humanity and reach Golconda through isolation...that means no Jyhad, no Ascension war, no technocracy etc...<br /> <br /> Otherwise, they take the responsibility for their actions and those of their beast. If you want to undermine that central aspect of VtM, feel free to do so. But don't pretend I'm the own doing the houseruling.<br /> <br /> The best one can hope from magic is the Red Sign ritual...which makes you turn back into a human (not what we're looking for...).</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;No u&quot;. How eloquent.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is, if you're making it so <i>every possible method</i> of resisting the Beast aside from greeting the sun is actually the Curse <i>letting</i> the vampire resist it better, it removes some amount of responsibility - their <i>fault</i>. That's at least as much a part of personal horror as &quot;I am slowly being remade into something terrible by an outside force over which I have no control&quot;. It's the aspect of &quot;what have I done, what have I made myself into&quot;.<br /> <br /> Moreover, in using that interpretation, I'm not focusedly and deliberatey disregarding what the merits in question actually say they entail.<br /> <br /> If you want to undermine that central aspect of VtM, feel free to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T00:54:44-07:00","id":977052,"title":"","content":"come on gize u kno u want 2 see atlas vampires<br /> <br /> fanged terminators in capes amirite<br /> <br