ss=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=977066#post977066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you want to see the beauty that is a Primium-armored and fanged terminator in a dracula cape?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I confess, I want cyber-vampires...and v20 does allow you to do that...that doesn't change the fact that it's stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T05:50:06-07:00","id":977141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=977072#post977072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I confess, I want cyber-vampires...and v20 does allow you to do that...that doesn't change the fact that it's stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beautiful you mean.<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, I cannot really see a lot of functions that a vampire can do for the Technocracy other than &quot;no Paradox&quot;, which is probably why I'm joking around with it, because the same function can be achieved with a bunch of Sleepers with guns and Mind shielding.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you're a Technocrat, you'll just kidnap people and use Arete + Cult if you want to do stuff with them, so your dice pool will be around 6-8 anyways because you'll presumably have a bunch of Conditioned Sleepers to help you with your endeavors. Furthermore, vampires need a constant supply of blood and have the whole &quot;might Frenzy and fuck up literally everything&quot; issue that a loyal Construct doesn't have. <br /> <br /> I mean, the closest example I've seen of this would be Rose Ashford from Panopticon Quest over at SV who is a clone of a Technocratic leader that has been xenografted to a bunch of vampire things and undergone Enlightenment, who mostly uses the whole &quot;vampire&quot; thing as a Focus for her Spheres.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:27:23-07:00","id":977343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=977141#post977141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the closest example I've seen of this would be Rose Ashford from Panopticon Quest over at SV who is a clone of a Technocratic leader that has been xenografted to a bunch of vampire things and undergone Enlightenment, who mostly uses the whole &quot;vampire&quot; thing as a Focus for her Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the Progenitor-engineered Lasombra bloodline made by repeatedly Embracing defective clones.<br /> <br /> Or the time the Former Prince LaCroix had his backers in the SPD make the Sheriff into a horrifying cybernetic war machine, his heart and brain the only portions of his vampiric flesh remaining within the horrormurderbot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T20:08:59-07:00","id":977555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=977066#post977066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Don't you want to see the beauty that is a Primium-armored and fanged terminator in a dracula cape?</div> </div> </div> </div>(Launches MD out an airlock)<br /> <br /> (Mouths &quot;no&quot; in the viewport)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T03:46:43-07:00","id":977676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=977555#post977555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Launches MD out an airlock)<br /> <br /> (Mouths &quot;no&quot; in the viewport)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Foolish Saur Ops! I am the ghost of Mage's past, the specter of silly crossover that lurks in the shadows of time! I am your Blood Treachery! Your Dirty Secrets of The Black Hand! You can never defeat me!<br /> <br /> Have I mentioned that I despise crossover.<br /> <br /> You can also have Primium werewolves if you want to?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=977343#post977343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the Progenitor-engineered Lasombra bloodline made by repeatedly Embracing defective clones.<br /> <br /> Or the time the Former Prince LaCroix had his backers in the SPD make the Sheriff into a horrifying cybernetic war machine, his heart and brain the only portions of his vampiric flesh remaining within the horrormurderbot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh right, I forgot those.<br /> <br /> That Lasombra Bloodline is pretty shitty though, what are they Potence, Celerity, Obtenebration that take extra damage from UV? I remember when they were considered against Yinzheng and everyone were like &quot;dude, she'll just switch to UV and laugh at us for wasting our requisitions.&quot;<br /> <br /> That thing with LaCroix was pretty cool though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":6042,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","user":"ManusDomine","date":". 09-28-2016, 06:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T10:19:37-07:00","id":978470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=976894#post976894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;No u&quot;. How eloquent.</div> </div> </div> </div>what?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=976894#post976894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm saying is, if you're making it so <i>every possible method</i> of resisting the Beast aside from greeting the sun is actually the Curse <i>letting</i> the vampire resist it better, it removes some amount of responsibility - their <i>fault</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they have little responsibility for their curse (except Tremere). They're still responsible for what they do with their curse.<br /> It's these aspects of their existence that gave rise to organizations such as the Sabbat (we are not responsible for being monsters, but responsible monsters nonetheless), and the Laibon (who can give up on their power from <i>Orun</i> to resist the beast with <i>Aye</i>).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=976894#post976894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, in using that interpretation, I'm not focusedly and deliberatey disregarding what the merits in question actually say they entail.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really wanted to avoid discussing this point at all costs. Because, last time I did something similar, I got banned...<br /> so...but...you know, I'd like to carry on to the conversation...screw the mods.<br /> <br /> But, before I go deeper, let me remind you that, while v20 rules allows you to play curse-less paradox-less brainwashed vampires. These same vampires can also find a way to break their hunger, their clan curse, their shackles, use magick (yes &quot;magick&quot;, not &quot;magic&quot;), bloat the sun, turn the tide, lower their generation with an attainable ritual, raise an army of mages, take over the technocracy and one-punch an Archmage...<br /> <br /> is this the kind of vampire you want in your game?...simply put, I won't talk about v20. Like I said in my previous posts, there is no curse in V20. And, like the previous vampire vs mage thread pointed out: v20 vampires are broken as fuck.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Calm Heart, V20 p. 485.</b> Exception here. This one existed in Revised along with the Guide to Technocracy so...<br /> <br /> It's obviously a permutation of the curse, it's a natural state where the beast's urges are weaker. Brujah cannot take this merit (their beast is stronger instead of weaker).<br /> <br /> It's not an aspect of the vampire's personality, this is supported by the Trujah, Unifiers (PatIV), Martyrs (Redemption) and Necronomists (Death and the Soul) which are known for their coldness and extraordinary calm, yet they get no bonus in resisting the beast (unless they take this merit).<br /> <br /> <b>Lion-Hearted, Player's Guide to the High Clans, p. 204.</b> I believe it's a permutation of the curse, which is similar to the Laibon curse. Laibon don't have self-control, they have the Aye score (which is a substitute to humanity that can go up to 10) to resist the beast (but they pay a big price for it).<br /> <br /> <b>Flock, Player's Guide to the Low Clans, p. 186.</b>permutation. The curse is weak, the beast is not powerful enough to override the I.F.F, which, normally, is only possible for vampires on Instinct (who can let the beast take over while staying conscious).<br /> <br /> <b>Controlled Thirst, Player's Guide to the High Clans, p. 203. </b>Permutation. Hunger comes from the curse, hunger is dulled, the beast's hunger is dulled. It seems like a different version of prey exclusion and methuselah's thirst.<br /> <br /> Note that, while it does mean you frenzy less for blood, it also means the beast is going to be a freaking killing machine when frenzying for anything else.<br /> <br /> I would count it as a flaw for vampires on Instinct (especially Road of Sin). Harder to tame the beast. If you can't satisfy the blood lust with human blood, he's going to satisfy it some other way (murder...).<br /> <br /> <b>Philosophical Humanist, Road of Humanity p. 73.</b> This one doesn't look like a permutation. But at the same time, is not an aspect of the vampire's personality.<br /> <br /> It does seem similar to calm heart, especially since Brujah can't take the merit (so it could be a permutation). And several Paths are all about judicious application of reason and do not believe in neither Caine nor God, yet they get no bonus against frenzy, so...I don't know, it doesn't make sense.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-29-2016, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T12:54:21-07:00","id":978547,"title":"","content":"Are you sure you are looking at the same V20 as the rest of us? I think they still have the Curse and, quite frankly, are arguably a little weaker than they were in Revised (Celerity and Potence are weaker, for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:09:20-07:00","id":978612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=978547#post978547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure you are looking at the same V20 as the rest of us? I think they still have the Curse and, quite frankly, are arguably a little weaker than they were in Revised (Celerity and Potence are weaker, for example).</div> </div> </div> </div>have you checked the mechanics in Lore of the Clans?<br /> Have you checked v20 Guide to the Tal'mahe'ra?<br /> <br /> no stasis, frenzy resistance, can do magick, Baali can remove the beast, Brujah can fix their weakness...even the Ventrue can have their prey exclusion shifted.<br /> <br /> Now, where's the curse in all that?<br /> <br /> can't walk on sunlight?...such an awful curse, right?<br /> <br /> Yes, &quot;no curse&quot; was hyperbole, but you get the meaning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-29-2016, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:14:00-07:00","id":978666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=977141#post977141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more serious note, I cannot really see a lot of functions that a vampire can do for the Technocracy other than &quot;no Paradox&quot;, which is probably why I'm joking around with it, because the same function can be achieved with a bunch of Sleepers with guns and Mind shielding.</div> </div> </div> </div>With enslaved Cainites or Garou, NWO would have access to powerful agents without having to call in Iteration-X or the Progenitors. Though one could make the case that those two Conventions would still be needed to create and main the control mechanisms...<br /> But assuming that the control/enslavement would be done mainly through NWO mastery of the mind and psyche, it could be good for making NWO more self-reliable and cementing their place as the leaders of the Technocracy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T01:14:40-07:00","id":978914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=978666#post978666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With enslaved Cainites or Garou, NWO would have access to powerful agents without having to call in Iteration-X or the Progenitors. Though one could make the case that those two Conventions would still be needed to create and main the control mechanisms...<br /> But assuming that the control/enslavement would be done mainly through NWO mastery of the mind and psyche, it could be good for making NWO more self-reliable and cementing their place as the leaders of the Technocracy!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good point, especially Garou with Technocratic gear would be terrifying and could show those casuals in Pentex how a <i>real </i>abomination of science looks.<br /> <br /> Brb writing Glass Walker/Syndicate elite strike force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T00:41:54-07:00","id":979545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=978914#post978914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brb writing Glass Walker/Syndicate elite strike force.</div> </div> </div> </div>ON L'ENCULE LE CONSENSUS...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T03:58:51-07:00","id":979577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=978612#post978612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> can do magick</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did you find that?<br /> The closest thing I can think of are the Idran associated with the Black hand, and their oldest Yamasattva, which are probably liches more than anything. They're not vampires. (Though they are undead, but liches are Mage canon)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T12:05:29-07:00","id":979787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/969937-the-technocracy-and-indoctrination-of-the-none-awakned?p=979577#post979577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where did you find that?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was on the last tal'mahe'ra book, they had rules to do magick using blood familiars. Though, I'm not sure whether it's the vampire or the familiar that suffers paradox.<br /> I like what they wrote in the book:<br /> <br /> &quot;Vampires cannot use Awakened sorcery. This rule is<br /> supposedly as inviolable as vampiric damnation. However,<br /> this rule can be bent.&quot;<br /> <br /> OP is champion at bending the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 10-01-2016, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}